| row | mean | latent_sd | observation_sd | latent_lower | latent_upper | observation_lower | observation_upper |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| 1 | 0 | 0.632456 | 1.183216 | -1.239590 | 1.239590 | -2.319061 | 2.319061 |
| 2 | 0 | 0.632456 | 1.183216 | -1.239590 | 1.239590 | -2.319061 | 2.319061 |

\image(figures/gpr_repeated_queries.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Joint covariances for repeated queries. Diagonal observation noise changes the distribution of differences without changing the posterior mean or the off-diagonal latent dependence.)
\alttext(Two two-by-two heatmaps print their cell values. The latent matrix has 0.4 in every cell; the new-observation matrix has 1.4 on its diagonal and 0.4 off the diagonal.)

> Checking the theory

>> Finite prior limits and the exact noise increment

Shift the first example's responses to \((9,11)\). Its empirical mean is now ten,
while response scale, profiled signal variance and noise variance remain one, one and
one half. Translation changes the posterior mean by ten and leaves the covariance
unchanged. Over a grid extending well beyond the two training inputs, check

$$
 0\leq v_f(x)\leq1,\qquad v_{\mathrm{new}\ y}(x)-v_f(x)=1/2,\qquad
 \mu(x)\longrightarrow10,\quad v_f(x)\longrightarrow1.
$$
\alttext(Latent variance is bounded by the unit prior variance, new-observation variance exceeds it by exactly one half, and sufficiently distant posterior means and latent variances approach ten and one.)

The upper bound follows because the covariance reduction is nonnegative. The limits
follow from every RBF cross-covariance tending to zero. They are not a claim of
monotone variance in distance from the nearest observation. The future-observation
variance approaches 1.5, not one.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/gpr_prior_limits.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame data; data.add_column("x",std::vector<double>{0,1}); data.add_column("y",std::vector<double>{9,11});
  dm::stats::GaussianProcessRegressionOptions options;
  options.length_scale=1/std::sqrt(2*std::log(2.0)); options.noise_ratio=.5; options.standardize=false; options.jitter_ratio=0;
  const dm::stats::GaussianProcessRegression gp(data,"y ~ x",options);
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame query; query.add_column("x",dm::seql(-4,5,201).values()); const auto p=gp.prediction_table(query);
  const auto& x=query.numeric_column("x").values(); auto mean=dm::graphics::RPlot::create(), variance=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  mean.lines(x,p.numeric_column("observation_lower").values(),"New-y bounds",{220,90,35})
    .lines(x,p.numeric_column("observation_upper").values(),"",{220,90,35})
    .lines(x,p.numeric_column("latent_lower").values(),"Latent bounds",{150,70,180})
    .lines(x,p.numeric_column("latent_upper").values(),"",{150,70,180})
    .lines(x,p.numeric_column("mean").values(),"Mean",{37,99,235},3).points({0,1},{9,11},"Observed",{70,70,70},5)
    .abline_h(10,{110,110,110}).title("The mean returns to its specified prior").x_label("Query x").y_label("Response").y_limits(6.8,15);
  variance.lines(x,dm::pow(dm::Vector<>(p.numeric_column("latent_sd").values()),2).values(),"Latent variance",{37,99,235},3)
    .lines(x,dm::pow(dm::Vector<>(p.numeric_column("observation_sd").values()),2).values(),"New-y variance",{220,90,35},3)
    .abline_h(1,{110,110,110}).abline_h(1.5,{150,150,150})
    .title("Variance saturates; noise remains").x_label("Query x").y_label("Squared response").y_limits(0,2.2);
  auto layout=dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2);layout.add(mean).add(variance);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");layout.size(1100,490).fit_panels().save_svg("build/gpr_prior_limits.svg");
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame selected;selected.add_column("x",std::vector<double>{0,.5,1,5,10});auto result=gp.prediction_table(selected);
  result.add_column("x",selected.numeric_column("x").values());
  std::print("{}\n",result.select({"x","mean","latent_sd","observation_sd","observation_lower","observation_upper"}).to_md(6));
}
```
